-The tests need development tools, installed from a lock file into the `.venv` folder so that nothing else on your computer changes. The commands for Windows and Linux are in `docs/tests.md`; the test command itself is `python -m pytest -q`. Supported: Windows with Python 3.13 and `requirements-dev-win.txt`, or Linux x86_64 with Python 3.12 and `requirements-dev.txt`; any other combination was not tried. If pip prints a hash mismatch, you are using the wrong lock file or Python version for your computer. A full run was last timed at 16 minutes 33 seconds on an earlier, smaller set of tests (`docs/tests.md`, which says no log is shipped); it has not been timed on the current set, which is larger. The tests need a git clone (some tests read the list of tracked files with git).
